LINEAGE(7)                 TriadicFrameworks Manual                 LINEAGE(7)
================================================================================
NAME
       lineage - structural memory of triadic cycles, resonance propagation,
                 and schema-aligned state evolution in RTT

SYNOPSIS
       Lineage records:
           • triadic history
           • resonance-time propagation
           • structural transitions
           • schema validation events
           • package-level coherence markers

DESCRIPTION
       Lineage is the persistent structural memory of RTT. It records how
       triads evolve, how resonance-time propagates, and how schemas are
       satisfied across cycles.

       Lineage is not a log. It is a structural artifact:
           “This is how the system became what it is now.”

       Every triad contributes to lineage. Every resonance package depends
       on lineage. Every schema validates lineage.

       Without lineage, the system cannot maintain coherence across cycles.

PURPOSE
       Lineage serves four essential roles:

       1. Historical Record
              Captures the sequence of triadic actions and their structural
              effects.

       2. Resonance Propagation
              Tracks how resonance-time flows from one cycle to the next.

       3. Schema Validation
              Ensures that each triad and operator conforms to declared
              structural boundaries.

       4. Coherence Maintenance
              Prevents drift, fragmentation, or incoherent transitions.

WHY LINEAGE MATTERS
       • Triads alone are momentary.
       • Resonance-time alone is continuous.
       • Schemas alone are static.

       Lineage binds them together.

       It ensures:
           • continuity across cycles
           • structural integrity across patterns
           • reproducibility of results
           • interpretability of system evolution

       Lineage is the backbone of RTT coherence.

LINEAGE STRUCTURE
       Lineage entries typically include:
           • triad identifier
           • timestamp (RT, not wall-clock)
           • resonance-state snapshot
           • schema references
           • operator metadata
           • structural transitions
           • closure integration notes

       WRSADC writes lineage entries during dispatch.

INTERACTION WITH TRIADS
       Each triad contributes a lineage arc:

           P1 (begin)
               → lineage: context established
           P2 (transform)
               → lineage: resonance shift recorded
           P3 (close)
               → lineage: integration and sealing

       A triad without lineage is incomplete.

INTERACTION WITH RESONANCE-TIME
       Lineage is the discrete record of continuous resonance-time flow.

       Resonance-time defines:
           • how lineage propagates
           • how cycles influence each other
           • how coherence is maintained

       Lineage is the “breadcrumb trail” through RT-space.

INTERACTION WITH SCHEMAS
       Schemas define what lineage *should* look like.

       Lineage records what lineage *actually* is.

       Schema checks ensure:
           • allowed transitions
           • valid resonance states
           • correct operator signatures
           • coherent triadic patterns

       If lineage violates schema expectations, WRSADC halts dispatch.

INTERACTION WITH RESONANCE PACKAGES
       A resonance package is coherent only if its lineage is coherent.

       Packages must include:
           • lineage-schema
           • structural-schema
           • resonance-schema

       Lineage ensures that packages remain stable across:
           • modules
           • agents
           • dispatch layers
           • simulation cycles

LINEAGE STORAGE
       Shell-level:
           $THREEPAK_STATE
           $THREEPAK_LOG

       Engine-level:
           internal resonance-state maps

       Schema-level:
           lineage-schema definitions

       Lineage is both external (files) and internal (RT-space).

USAGE
       Lineage is not edited manually.

       It is produced automatically by:
           • 3-Pack primitives
           • WRSADC dispatch
           • Engine propagation
           • schema validation layers

NOTES
       Lineage is the structural memory of RTT. Without lineage, triads lose
       continuity, resonance-time loses coherence, and schemas lose meaning.

